    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">substantīvus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		substantia, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>self-existent</i>, <i>substantive</i>
			(post - class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In
			gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Prax. 26</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. adv. Hermog.
			26</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In gram.: substantivum verbum, <i>the substantive
			verb</i>, i.e. sum (a transl. of the Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπαρκτικόν</span>), <i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 812
					<i>fin.</i></span></i> P.</div>
